<div id="recipe-83593-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-83593-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="83593"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83593-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Break the feta into large chunks and place it in the bowl of a food processor fitted with the metal blade.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing the making of whipped feta cheese spread in a food processor." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/feta-Greek-yogurt-dip.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83593-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add in the Greek yogurt and lemon zest.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83593-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Turn the food processor on. While it is blending, slowly add olive oil through the tube.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83593-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Blend until smooth, no more than 40-45 seconds, stopping halfway through to scrape the sides as needed.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing the whipped feta in a food processor and in a serving platter with veggies." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Feta-cheese-dip-recipe.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83593-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Transfer to a bowl and garnish with fresh herbs. Finish with a light drizzle of olive oil and a sprinkle of sumac or red pepper flakes.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-83593-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes about 1 &frac12; to 1 &frac34; cups whipped feta, ideal for four servings. The nutritional values below are per serving and do not include calories from the optional vegetables and pita bread shown in the pictures.</li>
<li><strong>Feta:&nbsp;</strong>Use a mildly salty block of feta for the best whipped feta recipe.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:</strong> Transfer leftovers to an airtight container and store in the fridge for 3-4 days. Give it a stir before serving.</li>
<li><b>Troubleshooting Consistency and Texture:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You have two variables to consider here: </span><b>the amount of yogurt used</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and </span><b>the blending time</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">For </span><b>a thicker dip</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, use &frac12; cup of yogurt, as written in the recipe.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">For </span><b>a looser, more sauce-like, spreadable texture, </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">add &frac14; cup more (a total of &frac34; cup) yogurt.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><b>Too grainy?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Blend it a bit longer by stopping and scraping the sides a few times.</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></div>
